Theorem. On the sphere, every cocycle is a coboundary.

Cover the sphere by U1, U2, U3 and U4, the faces of a tetrahedron.
The transition on U1 and U2 is 1.
The transition on U2 and U3 is 2.
The transition on U1 and U3 is 3.
The transition on U1 and U4 is 0.
The transition on U2 and U4 is -1.
The transition on U3 and U4 is -3.
The triple overlap of U1, U2 and U3 is not empty.
The triple overlap of U1, U2 and U4 is not empty.
The triple overlap of U1, U3 and U4 is not empty.
The triple overlap of U2, U3 and U4 is not empty.
One checks the cocycle condition.
By gluing.
Sheafify.
Publish.
QED.
